Task 1: Define Cross-Cluster Deployment Strategies
Subtask 1.1: Understanding Multi-Cluster Architecture
First, let's examine the current cluster setup and understand the multi-cluster architecture.

Access the RHACM Hub Cluster
# Set the hub cluster context
oc config use-context hub-cluster

# Verify RHACM installation
oc get pods -n open-cluster-management
List Managed Clusters
# View all managed clusters
oc get managedclusters

# Get detailed information about managed clusters
oc describe managedclusters
Expected output should show two managed clusters: cluster-east and cluster-west.

Subtask 1.2: Create Placement Policies
Create placement policies to define where applications should be deployed.

Create a Namespace for Application Management
# Create namespace for our application
oc create namespace cross-cluster-apps
Define Placement Policy for Geographic Distribution
Create a file named placement-policy.yaml:

apiVersion: cluster.open-cluster-management.io/v1beta1
kind: Placement
metadata:
  name: geo-placement
  namespace: cross-cluster-apps
spec:
  numberOfClusters: 2
  clusterSets:
    - default
  predicates:
    - requiredClusterSelector:
        labelSelector:
          matchExpressions:
            - key: environment
              operator: In
              values: ["production", "staging"]
Apply the Placement Policy
# Apply the placement configuration
oc apply -f placement-policy.yaml

# Verify placement creation
oc get placement -n cross-cluster-apps
Subtask 1.3: Configure Cluster Labels
Label the managed clusters to support placement decisions.

Label the East Cluster
# Label cluster-east
oc label managedcluster cluster-east environment=production region=east

# Verify labels
oc get managedcluster cluster-east --show-labels
Label the West Cluster
# Label cluster-west
oc label managedcluster cluster-west environment=staging region=west

# Verify labels
oc get managedcluster cluster-west --show-labels
Task 2: Use GitOps to Automate Deployments Across Clusters
Subtask 2.1: Set Up Git Repository Structure
Create Application Repository Structure
# Create local directory structure
mkdir -p ~/cross-cluster-app/{base,overlays/{east,west}}
cd ~/cross-cluster-app
Create Base Application Manifests
Create base/deployment.yaml:

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: sample-app
  labels:
    app: sample-app
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: sample-app
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: sample-app
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: sample-app
        image: quay.io/redhat-developer/hello-world-nginx:latest
        ports:
        - containerPort: 8080
        env:
        - name: CLUSTER_REGION
          value: "default"
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: sample-app-service
spec:
  selector:
    app: sample-app
  ports:
  - port: 80
    targetPort: 8080
  type: ClusterIP
Create Kustomization Base
Create base/kustomization.yaml:

apiVersion: kustomize.config.k8s.io/v1beta1
kind: Kustomization

resources:
- deployment.yaml

commonLabels:
  app.kubernetes.io/name: sample-app
  app.kubernetes.io/version: v1.0.0
